        "original_id": "6d940fef-f055-5955-afa6-17ab2b4115e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yuh-Line Niou, Sheldon Silver, Alice Cancel, Joseph D. Morelle\n- Organizations: Democratic Party, New York State Assembly\n- Roles: Assembly member, Speaker, Majority Leader\n- Places: New York City, New York\n- Events: 2013 leadership appointment, 2015 arrest, 2016 Democratic primary\n\nFacts:\n- In January 2013, Speaker Sheldon Silver appointed Joseph D. Morelle as Majority Leader of the New York State Assembly.\n- In 1994, Sheldon Silver became Speaker of the New York State Assembly.\n- In 2015, Sheldon Silver’s tenure as Speaker of the New York State Assembly ended with his arrest on federal corruption charges.\n- In 2016, Yuh-Line Niou defeated Alice Cancel in the Democratic primary for a New York State Assembly seat.\n- Yuh-Line Niou is a Democratic Party member of the New York State Assembly for New York’s 65th district.\n- The New York State Assembly seat held by Yuh-Line Niou was previously held by Sheldon Silver.\n- Sheldon Silver, born on February 13, 1944, is a former lawyer and Democratic Party politician from New York City.",
